@* NewMemberAccountPage: creates a local account and adds it to a project in one step, at
   "/projects/{id}/members/account". Whoever may administer the project (a system administrator or a project admin of
   it) types a user name, a display name and chooses whether the person becomes a project admin. The application
   generates a temporary password and shows it once on this page; nobody types or chooses it. The person has to choose
   a new password at the first sign-in. Anybody else sees the not-found message of a missing project.

   Presentation only; state and event handling live in NewMemberAccountPage.razor.cs. The temporary password lives
   only in the memory of this page instance until "Done" is used or the page is left; it is never written to a log, an
   audit entry or the address. The data-interactive marker on the root flips to "true" once the live circuit is
   connected.

   Human factors: (a) three inputs on one narrow form; (b) the page is reached from the rare "Create a new account"
   button of the add member page, so the common case (an account that exists) is not burdened by it; (c) the result
   box says what to do with the password (give it to the person now) and that it cannot be shown again.

   The page body is inside SessionGate, which replaces it with a "Session ended" message when the user is no longer
   valid while the page is open. *@
@page "/projects/{ProjectId:int}/members/account"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@attribute [Authorize]

<PageTitle>Create account - ReviewCenter</PageTitle>

<SessionGate>
<main class="page narrow" data-testid="new-account-page" data-interactive="@InteractiveMarker">
    <nav class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/projects" data-testid="breadcrumb-projects-link">Projects</a>
        @if (Project is not null)
        {
            <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <a href="/projects/@ProjectId" data-testid="breadcrumb-project-link">@Project.Name</a>
            <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <a href="/projects/@ProjectId/members/new" data-testid="breadcrumb-add-member-link">Add member</a>
            <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <span aria-current="page">Create account</span>
        }
    </nav>

    @if (!Loaded)
    {
        <p class="muted" data-testid="new-account-loading">Loading...</p>
    }
    else if (Project is null)
    {
        <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="project-not-found">Project @ProjectId does not exist.</p>
    }
    else if (Created is not null)
    {
    <h1>Account created</h1>
    <section class="card">
        <div class="notice" role="status" data-testid="new-account-password-box">
            <p>
                <strong>Give this temporary password to @Created.Member.DisplayName now. It is shown only once.
                They must choose a new password when they first sign in.</strong>
            </p>
            <p>User name:
                <code class="mono" data-testid="new-account-username-value">@Created.Member.Username</code></p>
            <p>Temporary password:
                <code class="mono" data-testid="new-account-password-value">@Created.TemporaryPassword</code></p>
            <p>
                <button type="button" class="outline small" data-testid="copy-account-password-button"
                        @onclick="CopyPasswordAsync">Copy</button>
                <span class="muted" role="status" data-testid="account-password-copy-status">@CopyStatus</span>
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="plan-actions">
            <button type="button" data-testid="done-account-button" @onclick="Done">Done</button>
        </div>
    </section>
    }
    else
    {
    <h1>Create account</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">Create a new account for a person who does not have one, and add it to this project.</p>

    <section class="card">
        @if (ErrorMessage is not null)
        {
            <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="new-account-error">@ErrorMessage</p>
        }
        <form data-testid="new-account-form" @onsubmit="CreateAccountAsync">
            <div class="field">
                <label for="new-account-username">User name</label>
                <input id="new-account-username" type="text" maxlength="@ReviewLimits.MaxUsernameLength"
                       autocomplete="off"
                       data-testid="new-account-username-input" @bind="Username" @bind:event="oninput" />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label for="new-account-display-name">Display name</label>
                <input id="new-account-display-name" type="text" maxlength="@ReviewLimits.MaxDisplayNameLength"
                       autocomplete="off"
                       data-testid="new-account-display-name-input" @bind="DisplayName" @bind:event="oninput" />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label>
                    <input type="checkbox" data-testid="new-account-admin-checkbox" @bind="AsProjectAdmin" />
                    Project admin
                </label>
                <p class="muted hint">A project admin also manages the members and repositories of this project.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label>
                    <input type="checkbox" data-testid="new-account-auditor-checkbox" @bind="AsAuditor" />
                    Auditor (read-only)
                </label>
                <p class="muted hint">An auditor can read everything in this project and its audit trail, but cannot change anything or review.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="muted hint">A temporary password is generated and shown once, after you create the account.</p>
            <div class="plan-actions">
                <button type="submit" data-testid="new-account-submit">Create account</button>
                <a class="action outline" href="/projects/@ProjectId/members/new"
                   data-testid="new-account-cancel">Cancel</a>
            </div>
        </form>
    </section>
    }
</main>
</SessionGate>
